Acceptance criterion: SRS-NFR-01/AC-05

Verified on 2026-04-02.

Evidence:
- `README.md:150-185` reduces navigation sprawl by grouping docs into "Start
  Here", "Root Contracts", and "Focused Guides", with `docs/aws.md` acting as
  the canonical AWS entry point.
- `docs/hosted.md:7-10` and `docs/hosted.md:113-126` now point AWS production
  readers to `docs/aws.md` instead of duplicating the full operator narrative.
- `docs/cloud.md:8-14` turns the cloud guide into a lane matrix with explicit
  links to `aws.md`, `hosted.md`, and `pvm.md`.
- `docs/pvm.md:7-9` narrows the PVM guide to the host-kit and artifact-kit
  contract and sends operator readers to `docs/aws.md`.
- `website/docs/reference/foundational-docs.mdx:11-25` adds `docs/aws.md` to
  the foundational-doc reference list so the public site points back at the
  same canonical doc.

Conclusion:
- The refreshed docs reduce duplication and improve navigation through
  deliberate cross-links around the AWS/PVM path.
